cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ScaleLab or its dataset, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ScaleLab: a measurement lab for reinforcement learning on small language models"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - given-names: Soheil
    family-names: Sanati Moutaban
    affiliation: Argo Navis Lab
repository-code: "https://github.com/Argo-Navis-Lab/scalelab"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  ScaleLab measures how much reinforcement learning improves small language models as compute
  grows, and how that changes with model size. It prices every run before it starts with a
  calibrated cost model, watches it with per-step telemetry and anomaly detectors, compares
  algorithms at equal compute, and reports bootstrap confidence intervals over seeds and
  problems.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - language models
  - scaling laws
  - GRPO
  - cost model
references:
  - type: data
    title: "scalelab-runs"
    authors:
      - given-names: Soheil
        family-names: Sanati Moutaban
    url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/argo-navis-research-laboratory/scalelab-runs"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
